# Build context excludes — added to speed up `docker build`.
#
# DO NOT add `bin/` here. The release image is built from Dockerfile.binary,
# whose `COPY bin/kite-$TARGETARCH ./kite` reads the prebuilt binary from THIS
# context. If bin/ is excluded, Kaniko does not fail — it logs "No files to
# copy" and silently ships an image WITHOUT /app/kite, so the pod crash-loops
# with `exec: "/app/kite": no such file or directory` (StartError, exitCode 128).
# (`static`/`kite` are safe to exclude: the frontend is embedded into the binary
# via go:embed, so Dockerfile.binary needs only bin/kite-$TARGETARCH.)
**/node_modules
ui/dist
static
kite
*.db
.git
.github
e2e
docs
test-results
*.log
